      {
        "basis": "estimate: the IEA finds about 70% of fossil methane (nearly 85 Mt CH4, roughly 2.4 Gt CO2e) abatable with existing technology and about 30% (35 Mt CH4) at no net cost at 2025 prices (Global Methane Tracker 2026). Payments buy speed and verification where capital, not price, is the barrier; no-cost tons raise additionality questions, so they need jurisdiction-wide baselines",
        "cost_2035_bn": [
          0.8800000000000001,
          3.75,
          12.25
        ],
        "id": "methane",
        "label": "Oil, gas and coal-mine methane abroad: results payments to producers and regulators, verified by satellite and measurement",
        "mt_2035": [
          100,
          200,
          350
        ],
        "price": [
          8,
          15,
          25
        ]
      },
      {
        "basis": "sourced range: LEAF Coalition purchases jurisdictional credits, reported $10 a ton floor; Nepal's January 2026 agreement is up to 4 Mt for up to $55M (about $14 a ton); Ghana and Costa Rica (2023) over $60M. Jurisdictional accounting addresses leakage better than project credits; permanence needs buffers",
        "cost_2035_bn": [
          0.66,
          3.75,
          14.7
        ],
        "id": "forests",
        "label": "Jurisdictional forest results (national or state programs, ART-TREES style), with Indigenous and local community safeguards",
        "mt_2035": [
          50,
          150,
          300
        ],
        "price": [
          12,
          20,
          35
        ]
      },
      {
        "basis": "estimate: ADB's first ETM deal (Cirebon-1, 660 MW) targets retirement in 2035 instead of 2042 and up to 30 Mt avoided over 15 years; its financial terms are undisclosed",
        "cost_2035_bn": [
          0.8250000000000001,
          3.75,
          14.0
        ],
        "id": "coal",
        "label": "Early coal retirement and grid results contracts (Energy Transition Mechanism and JETP style)",
        "mt_2035": [
          50,
          100,
          200
        ],
        "price": [
          15,
          30,
          50
        ]
      },
      {
        "basis": "sourced: Switzerland's bilateral purchases about $36 a ton; vendor indications $30-50. As of May 2026, 128 bilateral agreements but only five completed transfers (65,000 ITMOs): the market barely exists yet",
        "cost_2035_bn": [
          0.66,
          2.5,
          8.399999999999999
        ],
        "id": "itmo",
        "label": "Article 6.2 programs: renewables, efficiency, e-mobility and industry, bilateral with corresponding adjustments",
        "mt_2035": [
          20,
